6. Feature requirements

6.1 Flight search
Core feature
Users can enter origin, destination, and travel date to search available flight offers.
Display airline, flight number, departure and arrival details, duration, and price when provided.
Use the Amadeus API for supported flight searches.
Handle invalid inputs, empty results, and API failures.

6.2 Flight status
Core feature
Users can enter a flight number to view the latest available flight information.
Flight number, airline, origin, and destination.
Scheduled and estimated departure and arrival times.
Status such as scheduled, active, delayed, or cancelled when supplied by the provider.
Last-updated information where available.

6.3 Live aircraft tracking
Core feature
Users can view aircraft locations on an interactive map.
Display aircraft markers from actual latitude and longitude data.
Show relevant flight details when a marker is selected.
Display the data's last-update time when available.
Show an explicit unavailable state if position data cannot be retrieved.

6.4 AI travel assistant
Core feature
Users can ask questions about their flight and receive practical travel guidance.
Multilingual input and responses.
Explain flight updates in simple language.
Suggest next steps for delays, cancellations, and missed connections.
Use available flight data as context.
Clearly distinguish verified information from general advice.

6.5 Authentication and saved trips
Supporting feature
Sign up, log in, and log out using Supabase Auth.
Save flights to a user's account.
View and remove saved trips.
Restrict private trip records to their owner.
7. User flow
Open AeroMate
Dashboard and flight search
Search for a flight
Enter flight number or search route
View flight information
Status, times, and aircraft position if available
Ask the AI assistant
Understand updates and get next-step guidance
Save the trip
Optional, for authenticated users
